[Weak Randomness] (sim-review): 0x1fd07693355ac7f1c29d2fc2bbc390fc0d5ad2ee used a block-environment value (block.timestamp/number/prevrandao/gaslimit/basefee) as the operand of a modulo/bitmask/comparison at pc 2084 (SWC-120). Such values are predictable by whoever watches the pending transaction and influenceable by the block producer, so any winner/lottery/selection logic built on them can be gamed.

[Fund Loss] (sim-confirmed): Anyone can earn 0.100 native tokens by interacting with the provided contracts

[Unchecked ecrecover(0)] (sim-confirmed): 0x1fd07693355ac7f1c29d2fc2bbc390fc0d5ad2ee called ecrecover() at pc 2075 with an invalid signature (recovered the zero address), and the call succeeded anyway -- likely missing a `require(signer != address(0))` check, which is exploitable if the compared value was never initialized.

[Unbounded Loop] (sim-review): 0x1fd07693355ac7f1c29d2fc2bbc390fc0d5ad2ee's loop at pc 2740 iterated 17 times this call, up from a previous max of 12 -- its trip count is GROWING across separate calls, meaning it's bounded by a storage value that only ever increases, not by calldata or a fixed constant. Gas cost for EVERY future call through this loop keeps rising as more state accumulates, until it eventually exceeds the block gas limit and the function becomes permanently unusable (unbounded-loop-over-growing-storage gas-griefing DoS). Heuristic: a loop can also grow once for a legitimate reason (e.g. a bigger caller-supplied length); this is only reported after the SAME loop grows repeatedly with no such explicit driver.

[Weak Randomness] (sim-review): 0x1fd07693355ac7f1c29d2fc2bbc390fc0d5ad2ee used a block-environment value (block.timestamp/number/prevrandao/gaslimit/basefee) as the operand of a modulo/bitmask/comparison at pc 2084 (SWC-120). Such values are predictable by whoever watches the pending transaction and influenceable by the block producer, so any winner/lottery/selection logic built on them can be gamed.

